\b Using Trigonometry\
\

\b0  \'95 Drag the red dot along the circle to display the angle, sinus and cosinus values.\
 \'95 When you stop dragging the red dot, sinus and cosinus coordinates are displayed.\
 \'95 When you drag the red dot clockwise, starting from (1,0), the dot and angle turn to blue, meaning you're using the negative orientation. Click on (1.0) to restore default (positive) orientation. \
\
